# Marker: this is a HYBRID collector. It has a Dockerfile (the Camoufox
# `download` / `vnc-login` image) AND needs a host venv (`load`,
# `prune`, `recompress` run on the host). With this file present the
# Makefile builds both, and tests on the host venv; without it, a
# Dockerfile would make build and test Docker-only.
#
# Why host-side load needs a venv (unlike a pure-stdlib loader): bronze
# HTML/CSV artefacts are zstd-compressed, and load.py decompresses
# them IN Python (fidelity-web's silver is SQLite, not DuckDB — there is
# no engine to stream .zst natively), so the host interpreter needs the
# `zstandard` package. The venv also carries pdfplumber for the 529 /
# trust statement-PDF parsing the loader does host-side.
